dFeedback_xml>&lt;text&gt;You got &lt;/text&gt;&lt;val id="percent"/&gt;&lt;text&gt;% for this marked interaction.&lt;/text&gt;</markedFeedback_xml><showPrefix>true</showPrefix><prefixActivityLevel>false</prefixActivityLevel><prefixStartIndex /><showPrefixes>false</showPrefixes><blankMinWidth>200</blankMinWidth><blankMaxWidth>650</blankMaxWidth><question_xml><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>In the original casting for the film, Tom Hinks [was to have played] the role of Christopher Columbus, but he pulled out at the last minute and Lou Caprison stepped in to take his place. (&lt;i&gt;play&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/1421.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>In the original casting for the film, Tom Hinks &lt;b&gt;was to have played&lt;/b&gt; the role of Christopher Columbus, but he pulled out at the last minute and Lou Caprison stepped in to take his place.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Mr Lee walked into the crowded office and began to announce the reorganisation of the company. On hearing that she [was to be transferred] to the New York office, Andrea began to protest. (&lt;i&gt;transfer&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/1422.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Mr Lee walked into the crowded office and began to announce the reorganisation of the company. On hearing that she &lt;b&gt;was to be transferred&lt;/b&gt; to the New York office, Andrea began to protest.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Emma Frisk was appointed CEO of the perfume company in 1976, a position which she [was to hold] until her death in 1998, at the age of 69. (&lt;i&gt;hold&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/1423.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Emma Frisk was appointed CEO of the perfume company in 1976, a position which she &lt;b&gt;was to hold&lt;/b&gt; until her death in 1998, at the age of 69.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>true</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>true</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Robbie Martens [was to have flown] to the United States this month to promote the company's new range of smartphones, but his trip has been postponed due to illness. (&lt;i&gt;fly&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/1424.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Robbie Martens &lt;b&gt;was to have flown&lt;/b&gt; to the United States this month to promote the company's new range of smartphones, but his trip has been postponed due to illness.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>The receptionist told me that I [was to wait] outside until my name was called. (&lt;i&gt;wait&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/1425.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>The receptionist told me that I &lt;b&gt;was to wait&lt;/b&gt; outside until my name was called.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Talks in the Hague that [were to have set out] the basis for a peace treaty between the two countries have broken down. (&lt;i&gt;set out&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/1426.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Talks in the Hague that &lt;b&gt;were to have set out&lt;/b&gt; the basis for a peace treaty between the two countries have broken down.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>They [were to have left] this morning, but their plane was cancelled because of the heavy snow. (&lt;i&gt;leave&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/1427.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>They &lt;b&gt;were to have left&lt;/b&gt; this morning, but their plane was cancelled because of the heavy snow.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>I played the part that Mr Rowland [was to have taken] before his argument with the theatre manager. (&lt;i&gt;take&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/1428.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>I played the part that Mr Rowland &lt;b&gt;was to have taken&lt;/b&gt; before his argument with the theatre manager.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>I arrived at the hospital a few minutes before my appointment at eleven o'clock. But I [was to wait] a further two hours before seeing Dr Coulson. (&lt;i&gt;wait&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/1429.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>I arrived at the hospital a few minutes before my appointment at eleven o'clock. But I &lt;b&gt;was to wait&lt;/b&gt; a further two hours before seeing Dr Coulson.</modelAnswerString></question><question ignorePunctuation="false" ignoreCase="false"><ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun>false</ignoreCaseExceptIPronoun><ignorePunctuationWithExceptions>false</ignorePunctuationWithExceptions><text>Jimmy planned to spend six months in Australia, but he [was to return] home after just a month saying that he had run out of money. (&lt;i&gt;return&lt;/i&gt;)</text><label /><audioURL>learning_objects/assets/14210.mp3</audioURL><skipPrefix>false</skipPrefix><isExample>false</isExample><modelAnswerString>Jimmy planned to spend six months in Australia, but he &lt;b&gt;was to return&lt;/b&gt; home after just a month saying that he had run out of money.</modelAnswerString></question></question_xml><enableAudioOnChecked>false</enableAudioOnChecked><enableAudioOnClosed>true</enableAudioOnClosed><correctFeedback_str /><incorrectFeedback_str /><attemptsAllowed>1</attemptsAllowed></mcq_xml></params_xml><alignment>none</alignment><alignPercent>100</alignPercent><custom_style_name /><sharedTokenBankId /><is_sequential>False</is_sequential><is_compulsory>False</is_compulsory><states><state id="queued" visible="True" enabled="False" /><state id="in_progress" visible="True" enabled="True" /><state id="complete" visible="True" enabled="True" /><state id="checked" visible="True" enabled="True" /><state id="closed" visible="True" enabled="True" /></states></params></object><object linkID="background_image"><params><imageURL>learning_objects/assets/agu_filler.png</imageURL><horizontalAlign>center</horizontalAlign><ver